    Add community discoverability commands: announce and export
    
      - betat export creates a backup file of all records that can be
        checked for tampering (each record's hash is recalculated and must
        match).
      - betat announce sends a message to the central registry saying new
        records are ready to be checked. The registry doesn't have a real
        address to send this to yet, so this is configurable and does
        nothing until an operator sets it up.
      - Reviewers can optionally turn on auto-announce, so it fires
        automatically every time a submission is accepted.
      - Tests pass on both database types (SQLite and PostgreSQL).

